    <tests>
        <!-- FAIRe-ator layout, one assay: instrument from the workbook without its OBI code, linked by sample_name -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="3">
            <param name="input_file" value="faire_ncbi_two_assays.xlsx"/>
            <conditional name="runs">
                <param name="runs_by" value="assay"/>
                <param name="runs_values" value="ssu16sv4v5-emp"/>
            </conditional>
            <output name="sra_table">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_n_lines n="5"/>
                    <has_line line="sample_name&#009;library_ID&#009;title&#009;library_strategy&#009;library_source&#009;library_selection&#009;library_layout&#009;platform&#009;instrument_model&#009;design_description&#009;filetype&#009;filename&#009;filename2&#009;filename3&#009;filename4&#009;assembly&#009;fasta_file"/>
                    <has_text text="GOMECC4_27N_Sta1_DCM_A&#009;GOMECC16S_Plate4_53&#009;GOMECC4_27N_Sta1_DCM_A: ssu16sv4v5-emp metabarcoding of seawater metagenome in USA: Atlantic Ocean, east of Florida (27 N)&#009;AMPLICON&#009;METAGENOMIC&#009;PCR&#009;paired&#009;ILLUMINA&#009;Illumina MiSeq&#009;Metabarcoding of 16S rRNA (SSU prokaryote) gene V4-V5 region"/>
                    <has_text text="&#009;fastq&#009;GOMECC16S_Plate4_53_S341_L001_R1_001.fastq.gz&#009;GOMECC16S_Plate4_53_S341_L001_R2_001.fastq.gz&#009;"/>
                    <not_has_text text="OBI_"/>
                    <not_has_text text="ssu18sv9-emp"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
            <output name="config">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_text text="lib_id_selection_choice: all"/>
                    <has_text text="kept 4 run(s) with assay_name in: ssu16sv4v5-emp"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
            <output name="log">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_text text="removed ontology codes"/>
                    <has_text text="wrote 4 SRA row(s)"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <!-- All runs: each library holds both assays (the same lib_id, sample and files), so its rows are joined -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="3">
            <param name="input_file" value="faire_ncbi_shared_library.xlsx"/>
            <output name="sra_table">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_n_lines n="5"/>
                    <has_text text="GOMECC4_27N_Sta1_DCM_A&#009;GOMECC16S_Plate4_53&#009;GOMECC4_27N_Sta1_DCM_A: ssu16sv4v5-emp and ssu18sv9-emp metabarcoding of seawater metagenome"/>
                    <has_text text="2 assays in one library. ssu16sv4v5-emp: Metabarcoding of 16S rRNA (SSU prokaryote) gene V4-V5 region"/>
                    <has_text text="; ssu18sv9-emp: Metabarcoding of 18S rRNA (SSU eukaryote) gene"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
            <output name="log">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_text text="joined the rows of 4 libraries that hold several assays (ssu16sv4v5-emp and ssu18sv9-emp)"/>
                    <has_text text="4 lib_ids name several assays (e.g. GOMECC16S_Neg1); FAIRe takes a library to be one amplicon of a sample"/>
                    <has_text text="wrote 4 SRA row(s) for 4 libraries"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <!-- The same libraries with one lib_id per amplicon (library, assay and run, as the FAIRe mapper
             writes them): joined by their files, with the library's own name as library_ID -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="3">
            <param name="input_file" value="faire_ncbi_amplicon_libraries.xlsx"/>
            <output name="sra_table">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_n_lines n="5"/>
                    <has_text text="GOMECC4_27N_Sta1_DCM_A&#009;GOMECC16S_Plate4_53&#009;GOMECC4_27N_Sta1_DCM_A: ssu16sv4v5-emp and ssu18sv9-emp metabarcoding of seawater metagenome"/>
                    <not_has_text text="_ssu16sv4v5-emp_"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
            <output name="log">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_text text="joined the rows of 4 libraries that hold several assays (ssu16sv4v5-emp and ssu18sv9-emp)"/>
                    <has_text text="library_ID is each library's own name: the lib_id without its assay_name and seq_run_id (e.g. GOMECC16S_Neg1_ssu16sv4v5-emp_20220613_Amplicon_PE250 -> GOMECC16S_Neg1)"/>
                    <not_has_text text="name several assays"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <!-- All runs: this example reuses lib_id across assays with different files, so the tool stops with advice -->
        <test expect_exit_code="1" expect_failure="true">
            <param name="input_file" value="faire_ncbi_two_assays.xlsx"/>
            <assert_stderr>
                <has_text text="these library_ID values appear more than once"/>
                <has_text text="run the tool once per assay"/>
            </assert_stderr>
        </test>
        <!-- FAIRe-NOAA layout, two assays, instrument chosen on the form -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="3">
            <param name="input_file" value="faire_noaa_layout.xlsx"/>
            <param name="instrument_model" value="Illumina NovaSeq 6000"/>
            <output name="sra_table">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_n_lines n="11"/>
                    <has_text text="GU190706-CTD11-220&#009;GU190706-CTD11-220_Riaz_S1&#009;"/>
                    <has_text text="&#009;ILLUMINA&#009;Illumina NovaSeq 6000&#009;Metabarcoding of 12S rRNA (SSU mitochondria) gene V5-V6 region using PCR primers MiFish-U-F"/>
                    <not_has_text text="Illumina MiSeq"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
            <output name="log">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_text text="already has assay columns named by assay_name"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <!-- Samples already registered: accessions from a BioSample attributes table -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="3">
            <param name="input_file" value="faire_ncbi_two_assays.xlsx"/>
            <conditional name="runs">
                <param name="runs_by" value="assay"/>
                <param name="runs_values" value="ssu18sv9-emp"/>
            </conditional>
            <conditional name="link">
                <param name="link_by" value="accessions"/>
                <param name="accessions" value="biosample_accessions.tsv" ftype="tabular"/>
            </conditional>
            <output name="sra_table">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_n_lines n="5"/>
                    <has_line_matching expression="^biosample_accession\tlibrary_ID\ttitle\t.*"/>
                    <has_text text="SAMN37516094&#009;GOMECC16S_Plate4_53&#009;GOMECC4_27N_Sta1_DCM_A: ssu18sv9-emp"/>
                    <has_text text="SAMN37516589&#009;GOMECC16S_Neg1&#009;"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <!-- Accession table with unexpected column names: the unanswered question becomes a plain error -->
        <test expect_exit_code="1" expect_failure="true">
            <param name="input_file" value="faire_ncbi_two_assays.xlsx"/>
            <conditional name="runs">
                <param name="runs_by" value="assay"/>
                <param name="runs_values" value="ssu18sv9-emp"/>
            </conditional>
            <conditional name="link">
                <param name="link_by" value="accessions"/>
                <param name="accessions" value="accessions_odd_columns.tsv" ftype="tabular"/>
            </conditional>
            <assert_stderr>
                <has_text text="FAIRe2NCBI asked a question that this Galaxy tool does not answer"/>
                <has_text text="Which column should be used for BioSample accession?"/>
            </assert_stderr>
        </test>
        <!-- One sequencing run, runs not yet submitted -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="3">
            <param name="input_file" value="faire_ncbi_two_assays.xlsx"/>
            <conditional name="runs">
                <param name="runs_by" value="seq_run"/>
                <param name="runs_values" value="20220613_Amplicon_PE250"/>
            </conditional>
            <param name="associated" value="blank_only"/>
            <output name="sra_table">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_n_lines n="3"/>
                    <has_text text="GOMECC16S_Neg1"/>
                    <has_text text="GOMECC16S_Plate4_53"/>
                    <not_has_text text="GOMECC16S_Plate4_46"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
            <output name="log">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_text text="kept 2 run(s) with no associatedSequences; left out 1"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <!-- Single assay in project_level; unknown assay name stops with the list of assays -->
        <test expect_exit_code="1" expect_failure="true">
            <param name="input_file" value="faire_ncbi_single_assay.xlsx"/>
            <conditional name="runs">
                <param name="runs_by" value="assay"/>
                <param name="runs_values" value="MiFish"/>
            </conditional>
            <assert_stderr>
                <has_text text="no runs with assay_name 'MiFish'. Values in the workbook: ssu16sv4v5-emp"/>
            </assert_stderr>
        </test>
        <test expect_num_outputs="3">
            <param name="input_file" value="faire_ncbi_single_assay.xlsx"/>
            <output name="sra_table">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_n_lines n="5"/>
                    <has_text text="Metabarcoding of 16S rRNA (SSU prokaryote) gene V4-V5 region using PCR primers 515F-Y (GTGYCAGCMGCCGCGGTAA) and 926R (CCGYCAATTYMTTTRAGTTT) using protocol at https://doi.org/10.1111/1462-2920.13023"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
            <output name="log">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_text text="single assay 'ssu16sv4v5-emp'"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <!-- NA and N/A in associatedSequences mark runs as already submitted -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="3">
            <param name="input_file" value="faire_noaa_text_values.xlsx"/>
            <param name="associated" value="blank_only"/>
            <output name="sra_table">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_n_lines n="9"/>
                    <not_has_text text="GU190707-CTD13-310_MiFish_S31"/>
                    <not_has_text text="GU190707-CTD13-310_Riaz_S2"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
            <output name="log">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_text text="kept 8 run(s) with no associatedSequences; left out 2"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
    </tests>
    <help><![CDATA[
@CHECK_BEFORE_UPLOAD@

**What it does**

This tool turns the **experimentRunMetadata** sheet of a FAIRe workbook into an SRA metadata table
for the NCBI Submission Portal, with one row for each sequencing library. Upload it on the *SRA
metadata* tab of an SRA submission at https://submit.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov, then upload the fastq files
it lists.

FAIRe2NCBI normally asks you questions as it runs. In Galaxy, the tool answers them from the form.
It also writes a **config** file holding those answers, so that the same run can be repeated
outside Galaxy.

-----

**Inputs**

- **A FAIRe workbook** (.xlsx). experimentRunMetadata needs samp_name, assay_name, lib_id, filename
  and, for paired reads, filename2. projectMetadata gives each assay's target gene, primers,
  platform and instrument.
- **Which runs to include**, and whether to leave out runs that have already been submitted.
- **How to link each run to its BioSample.** Choose **sample_name** when you register the
  BioSamples in the same submission (using the table from **FAIRe2NCBI: BioSample**), or
  **BioSample accession** when the samples are already registered.

**Outputs**

- **SRA table**: one row for each library. The columns follow NCBI's SRA template, and title and
  design_description are built from sampleMetadata and projectMetadata. library_strategy,
  library_source and library_selection are set to AMPLICON, METAGENOMIC and PCR.
- **config**: the answers given to FAIRe2NCBI, as YAML.
- **log**: a record of what FAIRe2NCBI and the tool did.

-----

**Checks**

The tool stops, with a list of the problems, if a library_ID or file name appears more than once,
if a library has no file name, or if a library has no BioSample accession when you link by
accession.

FAIRe defines a library as "an amplicon of a sample with unique MIDs". This means a sequencing
library that holds several assays, such as amplicons pooled before indexing, has a row for each
assay, with the same sample and files. The tool joins these into one row, with a title and design
description that name every assay.

library_ID is the library's own name. The FAIRe mapper writes lib_id as the library name,
assay_name and seq_run_id (M097_16SFish_LerayCOI_Fish16S_AGRF_2024-12), and this tool takes the
assay and run off again (M097_16SFish_LerayCOI). Where names would then repeat, as for a library
sequenced in two runs, the tool keeps the run, or failing that the whole lib_id. A lib_id given to
several assays with the same files is accepted, with a note. If the same lib_id was used for
several assays with different files, give each row its own lib_id, or run the tool once for each
assay.

**Not included**

FAIRe2NCBI can also check fastq files for empty or corrupted files, and split the output by
BioProject with links to the fastq files. Both of these need the fastq files in a local folder, so
they are not part of this Galaxy tool.

@HELP_LAYOUT@

@HELP_FAIRE_GUIDE@

@HELP_FOOTER@
    ]]></help>
    <expand macro="citations"/>
</tool>
